Silence py3.14 DeprecationWarnings in the shipped entry points.

The chimera-py314 patch demotes upstream's warnings-as-errors to
'default', which prints each unique deprecation once — operator-
facing noise that drowns the transfer progress lines (codecs.open,
datetime.utcnow, pycurl getinfo etc. fire dozens of times across
the import graph).  The deprecations are upstream pkg5's to fix;
the operator can't act on them.

Applies after pkg5-chimera-py314.patch (alphabetical order).

--- a/src/pull.py
+++ b/src/pull.py
@@ -1730,6 +1730,7 @@

         # Make all warnings be errors.
         warnings.simplefilter('default')  # spike: py3.14 deprecations are not errors
+        warnings.filterwarnings('ignore', category=DeprecationWarning)
         import six
         if six.PY3:
                 # disable ResourceWarning: unclosed file
--- a/src/pkgrepo.py
+++ b/src/pkgrepo.py
@@ -2370,6 +2370,7 @@

         # Make all warnings be errors.
         warnings.simplefilter('default')  # spike: py3.14 deprecations are not errors
+        warnings.filterwarnings('ignore', category=DeprecationWarning)
         if six.PY3:
                 # disable ResourceWarning: unclosed file
                 warnings.filterwarnings("ignore", category=ResourceWarning)
